{"id":"87134d7f-f9de-4652-b0ab-ddb063249847","object":"chat.completion","created":1785008225,"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\n  \"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    if not isinstance(case, dict):\\n        raise ValueError('case must be a dict')\\n    if 'tokens' not in case or 'calls' not in case:\\n        raise ValueError('case must contain \\\"tokens\\\" and \\\"calls\\\"')\\n    tokens = case['tokens']\\n    calls = case['calls']\\n    if not isinstance(tokens, list) or not isinstance(calls, list):\\n        raise ValueError('tokens and calls must be lists')\\n    # Validate each call\\n    required_call_keys = {'call_id', 'start', 'end', 'score', 'replacement_tokens'}\\n    for c in calls:\\n        if not isinstance(c, dict):\\n            raise ValueError('each call must be a dict')\\n        if not required_call_keys.issubset(c.keys()):\\n            raise ValueError('call missing required keys')\\n        if not isinstance(c['start'], int) or not isinstance(c['end'], int):\\n            raise ValueError('start and end must be ints')\\n        if not isinstance(c['score'], (int, float)):\\n            raise ValueError('score must be numeric')\\n        if not isinstance(c['replacement_tokens'], list):\\n            raise ValueError('replacement_tokens must be a list')\\n        if not all(isinstance(t, str) for t in c['replacement_tokens']):\\n            raise ValueError('replacement_tokens items must be strings')\\n        if c['start'] < 0 or c['end'] > len(tokens) or c['start'] >= c['end']:\\n            raise ValueError('invalid interval')\\n    # Sort candidates: descending score, ascending start, ascending call_id\\n    sorted_calls = sorted(calls, key=lambda c: (-c['score'], c['start'], c['call_id']))\\n    selected = []\\n    for c in sorted_calls:\\n        s, e = c['start'], c['end']\\n        overlap = False\\n        for sel in selected:\\n            ss, se = sel['start'], sel['end']\\n            if s < se and ss < e:\\n                overlap = True\\n                break\\n        if not overlap:\\n            selected.append(c)\\n    # Order selected by start for output\\n    selected.sort(key=lambda c: c['start'])\\n    selected_call_ids = [c['call_id'] for c in selected]\\n    # Apply replacements from right to left\\n    result_tokens = list(tokens)\\n    for c in sorted(selected, key=lambda c: -c['start']):\\n        s, e = c['start'], c['end']\\n        repl = c['replacement_tokens']\\n        result_tokens = result_tokens[:s] + repl + result_tokens[e:]\\n    return {'selected_call_ids': selected_call_ids, 'tokens': result_tokens}\"\n}","reasoning_content":"We need to produce Python source code for solve(case) that implements the described logic. The output must be a JSON object with keys \"selected_call_ids\" (list of strings) and \"tokens\" (list of strings). The logic: given tokens list, calls list (each with call_id, start, end, score, replacement_tokens). Need to select calls greedily: sort by descending score, then start ascending, then call_id lexicographically? The description: \"Rank candidates by descending score, start position, then call ID.\" So descending score, then ascending start, then maybe ascending call ID? It says \"start position, then call ID\" – likely ascending for both. Then greedy: accept first call that does not overlap any already selected call. Overlap: intervals [start, end) inclusive? The start and end are indices into tokens list, likely half-open? In example: call a: start=1, end=3, so indices 1,2. call b: start=2, end=5 => indices 2,3,4. Overlap if intervals intersect. For greedy, reject if overlapping any selected. Then order accepted calls by source start (ascending) for reporting selected_call_ids. Then apply replacements from right to left: for each accepted call in descending order of start (or end) index, replace tokens[start:end] with replacement_tokens. Return final token list and the list of selected call IDs in order of start.\n\nAlso need to handle invalid cases: Raise ValueError if missing required fields or if inputs are not valid? The payload should have tokens and calls. calls each have call_id, start, end, score, replacement_tokens. Not specified types, but we'll assume valid.\n\nImplementation: def solve(case): case is dict. Extract tokens list, calls list. Validate that each call has required keys and types. Then sort calls: key = (-score, start, call_id). Then iterate, check overlap: for each selected call, if intervals intersect (start < selected_end and end > selected_start?). Since start and end are indices, we define interval [start, end) so overlap if max(start, selected_start) < min(end, selected_end). Use that. Select if no overlap. After selection, sort selected calls by start ascending for output order. Then to apply replacements, sort selected calls by start descending (or end descending) to avoid offset shifts. For each selected call (in descending start order), replace tokens[start:end] with replacement_tokens list. Then tokens = tokens[:start] + replacement_tokens + tokens[end:]. Build output: selected_call_ids ordered by start, tokens as the final list.\n\nReturn {\"selected_call_ids\": [id1, id2, ...], \"tokens\": tokens}.\n\nEdge cases: calls might have overlapping but we reject. If no calls selected, selected_call_ids empty, tokens unchanged. Replacements could be multiple tokens.\n\nAlso need to handle if replacement_tokens is list of strings. Ensure we copy tokens list before mutating.\n\nWe'll produce Python code. Must be a single function solve(case). No imports beyond standard library. Use def solve(case): ... Return dict.\n\nWe'll also raise ValueError if case is not dict, missing keys, or calls missing required fields. But according to task: \"Raise ValueError for an infeasible or structurally invalid case instead of silently repairing it.\" So we should validate.\n\nNow output as JSON with key \"implementation